35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The complaint log shows one house filed eleven of fourteen complaints. That's a lot.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The station block argued about sweeping within two years. Their bin house smells bad too.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,Supervised mornings take fifty minutes each. That's twenty per house a year. Manageable.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,The frontages are uneven. One is very narrow. A permanent build might not fit.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The subsidy covers forty percent, capped. Last year's shelters cost two hundred forty-eight thousand.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, if the frontages are uneven, a rotation might be hard. But the complaints...","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka, twenty hours a year is not too much. But the smell from the bin house worries me.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the subsidy helps, but the ledger shows thirty-four thousand a year in extra fees.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, the narrow frontage is only ninety centimetres. We can't put a big bin there.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, the extra fees are from open bags. We need a system that prevents that.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"If we rotate, the narrow house gets a turn. But the complaints suggest they hate it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"Maybe managed hours? If we only put out bins in a window, it's cleaner.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The filing requirements say a permanent build takes four months. That's a long wait.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,Managed hours mean someone has to watch. Who does that? I don't want to be the one.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,The ward filing is strict. A rotation needs a notice for every change. That's paperwork.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I think managed hours might be best. It's fair, and we can take turns watching.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. It keeps the corner clean and the smell down. I like the idea.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,The hours are defined. It's logical. I can accept this if the turns are clear.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"As long as I don't have to do all the watching, I'm okay. Let's vote.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,It balances the burden. I support this. Let us see if the others agree.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
